  "description": "OpenMotion — Apply a named design style to a short video: pick one of 21 style cards (Bauhaus, Swiss, Constructivism, Memphis, Pop Art, Risograph, Neo-Brutalism, Art Deco, Liquid Glass, Ink Wash, New Wave and more) or two layouts (Bento Grid, Masonry), each with a palette, open-licensed typefaces, five rules and signature motion, then plan, check and build the film so it reads as that style. Use when someone says \"make this in Bauhaus style\", \"give my launch video a Swiss look\", \"which design style fits this?\", \"my video has no taste\", or names any listed style. Produces a 10–20 second 1920x1080 HTML composition that shows the content through the style's rules, plus the checked plan file.",
